#---
# purpose: VR.5b — dbg boxes across the any extern ABI and narrows by spec on return
#---
#
# # vr5b_typed_print
#
# VR.5b — dbg boxes across the any extern ABI and narrows by spec on return
#
# ## Notes
#
# `dbg(x)` is `IO.inspect(x)`, which renders through `Kernel.inspect/1`, an
# `any` extern: typed scalar args are boxed before the call. The public
# `dbg(t) :: t` spec then drives return ABI selection, so typed callers
# get their scalar back at the wrapper return boundary. Float debug
# rendering is shared by the boxed path so `4.0` remains `4.0`.
def int_main() do
  dbg(42)
end

def float_main() do
  dbg(1.5 + 2.5)
end

def main() do
  int_main()
  float_main()
end
